                <pb facs="0468" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.30/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-08T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 9—12:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>10. Referring to the Legation’s telegram of November 26, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d427-f1"/> President this morning expressed a desire that the naval
                    affairs commission, which he has requested, be selected and sent to Peru as soon
                    as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
